==============================================================================
Q2  ZERO-INIT PLUMBING IDENTITY  (measures NO effect, by construction)
==============================================================================
Loads the W5-off checkpoint into a W5-ON model and zeroes the three new
weight COLUMNS. The forward pass must then be identical to W5-off. This
proves the block is wired where the model reads it. It is NOT evidence
that burial helps -- a zeroed column cannot help.

Naive "just switch the flag on" strict load -> RuntimeError:
   size mismatch for fc1_gcn.weight: copying a param with shape torch.Size([64, 52]) from checkpoint, the shape in current model is torch.Size([64, 55]).
   size mismatch for fc1_gat.weight: copying a param with shape torch.Size([64, 36]) from checkpoint, the shape in current model is torch.Size([64, 39]).

zero-init load: missing=0 unexpected=0

proteins compared: 28
max |dG(zero-init W5 on) - dG(W5 off)| = 4.434e+00
COLUMN-LEVEL IDENTITY: NOT ACHIEVABLE -- and the reason is a REAL
ARCHITECTURAL FINDING, not a bug in this script. Verified by forward hooks:
  fc1_gat / fc1_gcn outputs are BIT-IDENTICAL (max diff 0.000e+00), so the
  zero-padding of those two weight matrices is correct and the three new
  columns are provably unread -- zeroing the solvation columns in the DATA
  changes the output by exactly nothing.
  The divergence enters LATER, at inst_norm2. hydro_net.forward_gat takes a
  STRUCTURALLY DIFFERENT BRANCH when solv_dim is set: the residual
  `identity` becomes the PROJECTED x (after fc2_gat) instead of the raw
  36-dim input, because the wider input can no longer be added to a
  fixed-width output. That branch is chosen by the FLAG, not by the values.
CONSEQUENCE: --burial_features is NOT a pure feature addition. Turning it on
changes the GAT residual topology even when every burial value is zero, so
a W5-on run is NOT a controlled comparison against a W5-off checkpoint.
Any W5 factorial cell therefore confounds "burial information" with "moved
the GAT residual". This needs an honest control arm -- see W5_ON_DG.md.
REMINDER: this arm measures PLUMBING, never effect. It cannot say whether
burial improves dG. That question needs training (Q3, GPU).

